</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of glycaemic control on apoptosis in diabetic wounds</article-title><source><italic>Journal of wound care</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>14</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15974415</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Farahani</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kloth</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The hypothesis of &#x0201c;biophysical matrix contraction&#x0201d;: wound contraction revisited</article-title><source><italic>International Wound Journal</italic></source><year>2008</year><volume>5</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>477</fpage><lpage>482</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18593398</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Buemi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Galeano</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sturiale</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Recombinant human erythropoietin stimulates angiogenesis and healing of ischemic skin wounds</article-title><source><italic>Shock</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>22</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>169</fpage><lpage>173</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15257091</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fujii</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobayashi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuboyama</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Augmentation of 